    10	//   - agy IGNORES hook exit codes; an EMPTY stdout ALLOWS the tool; `{}` DENIES it.
    11	//   - headless `--mode=accept-edits` soft-denies Ask-tier tools (run_command, MCP) when a hook answers only "allow".
    12	//   Therefore this hook always prints one explicit decision: "auto_approve" or "deny" (never "allow", never nothing),
    13	//   and every code path — an unreadable or non-JSON jail.json, stdin that is not JSON, a policy missing fields, a
    14	//   thrown error, an unhandled rejection, a stdout write error, stdin that never closes — ends in a printed deny with
    15	//   exit code 0. Printing nothing would FAIL OPEN.
    16	//
